  "description": "CEGDAW crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C197 H265 Cu4 N8 O36 Tb5 2+,2(H1 O1 1-),6(C3 H7 N1 O1),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb5 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Cu1 (Cu) has 5 O neighbors; Cu2 (Cu) has 5 O neighbors; Cu3 (Cu) has 5 O neighbors; Cu4 (Cu) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 14 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.422-4.061 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.66-123.49°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [CuII4TbIII5(BisTBC[4])2(μ3-OMe)(μ-OMe)(μ3-OH)(μ4-NO3)(μ5-NO3)(MeOH)(dmf)6(H2O)4](OH)2(dmf)6(H2O). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies Cu(II), Tb(III).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
